Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Lesson 4 log \[CenterDot] Building our own: a transformer that expands \
tensor-algebra expressions\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"e4611010-6866-44bc-a064-3995620734fb"],

Cell["\<\
Written 2026-11-24 02:06 UTC by lesson4_build_your_own.nb. 9 of 9 checks pass.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7650947d-c902-422a-bb88-73be6a37e1f7"],

Cell["\<\
This lesson assembles Lessons 1\[Dash]3 on our own problem. Lesson 1: encoder\
\[Dash]decoder and beam search. Lesson 2: uniform tree sampling, prefix \
notation and verification by an exact oracle. Lesson 3: the transformer \
parts, shared embeddings, label smoothing and the warm-up schedule.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26fcc2e4-9f8b-4cb8-a131-baf9dbee988c"],

Cell["1. The task and the data", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b6b3082e-b8a0-4ee5-aedb-f1b1b77144ec"],

Cell["\<\
Expand: the source is an expression written as one would type it, the target \
is its full expansion in prefix notation. Trees are drawn uniformly with \
Algorithm 1 of Lample and Charton (Lesson 2), with 1 to 5 operators, each \
\:2a02 or \:2a01, over the atoms a, b, c, d. \:2a02 binds tighter than \
\:2a01, so only a \:2a01 inside a \:2a02 needs parentheses.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68f31c88-b7bd-42ed-bdf2-280c884e2835"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"source (infix)\"\>", "\<\"target (expansion, prefix)\"\>"},
    {
     TemplateBox[{"\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"a\"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"b\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"], 
     TemplateBox[{"\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"a\"", "\"b\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"]},
    {
     TemplateBox[{
      "\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"c\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"b\"", "\"\:2a02\"", 
       "\"(\"", "\"a\"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"c\"", "\")\"", "\"\:2a02\"", 
       "\"b\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"], 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"c\"", 
       "\"\:2a02\"", "\"b\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"a\"", "\"b\"", "\"\:2a02\"", 
       "\"c\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"b\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"c\"", "\"b\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"]},
    {
     TemplateBox[{
      "\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"c\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"c\"", "\"\:2a02\"", 
       "\"c\"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"d\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"], 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"c\"", 
       "\"\:2a02\"", "\"c\"", "\"c\"", "\"d\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"]},
    {
     TemplateBox[{
      "\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"d\"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"d\"", "\"\:2a01\"", 
       "\"d\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"(\"", "\"a\"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"a\"", 
       "\"\:2a02\"", "\"a\"", "\")\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"], 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"d\"", "\"\:2a01\"", "\"d\"", 
       "\"\:2a01\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"d\"", "\"a\"", "\"\:2a02\"", "\"d\"", 
       "\"\:2a02\"", "\"a\"", "\"a\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       GrayLevel[0.85]}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"fc82f4f1-2053-4ab6-9122-5846bee461d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the tree sampler reaches all 14 binary trees with 4 operators, about \
equally often (counts 950\[Ellipsis]1060 out of 14,000)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d422b38b-d92d-49f9-8875-cc91ce4db027"],

Cell["2. The oracle", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3338db60-8215-487c-b293-2139fcad8f43"],

Cell["\<\
An expression is a list of words, each word an ordered \:2a02-product of \
atoms. \:2a01 joins two lists; \:2a02 multiplies every word of the left by \
every word of the right, keeping their order (\:2a02 is not commutative). Two \
expressions are equal when their lists of words agree up to order (\:2a01 is \
commutative up to isomorphism). This is the check tnEquivalentQ makes in \
TensorNets.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e63daedd-a9c8-4ab0-b1e2-6a45a5d32005"],

Cell["\<\
words(x) = {x}     words(A \:2a01 B) = words(A) \[Union] words(B)     words(A \
\:2a02 B) = { u v : u \[Element] words(A), v \[Element] words(B) }\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"a1f46c99-7f14-4426-aa6f-1a9bcad053ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "(a\:2a01b)\:2a02c expands to a\:2a02c \:2a01 b\:2a02c, i.e. \:2a01 \:2a02 a \
c \:2a02 b c"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8533f1ca-381e-4035-afb2-7b226ae0cbb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the oracle accepts a\:2a02c \:2a01 b\:2a02c in either order, and rejects c\
\:2a02a \:2a01 c\:2a02b (the order of factors matters)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"119a9680-ec97-4210-a6b1-74ccfab19978"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "for 500 random pairs the target is a valid prefix tree equivalent to the \
source"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46102869-45a8-4669-b699-20ed543e17c3"],

Cell["3. The net, assembled from the parts of Lesson 3", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3aa2604a-2ee3-4731-94de-698e0f0c9bf2"],

Cell["\<\
The encoder\[Dash]decoder of Lesson 3: shared embeddings multiplied by \
\[Sqrt]d, sinusoidal positions, 2 encoder and 2 decoder layers with 4 heads, \
d = 32, dff = 128. Source and target share one vocabulary of 10 tokens, so \
one array serves both embeddings and the output projection. The decoder reads \
the target without its last token (teacher forcing) and is trained to predict \
it without its first, against label-smoothed targets (\[Epsilon] = 0.1), with \
Adam (\[Beta]\:2082 = 0.98) and the warm-up schedule (400 steps).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bbd3c669-c894-4ec9-b71f-72f016be1b45"],

