Cell["\<\
Training took 211 s for 40 rounds. The loss cannot reach 0: with label \
smoothing its floor is the entropy of the smoothed target.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5c5ba3c-b489-4404-ab7a-8b41ad361cb9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the training loss fell by more than half (from 1.5 to 0.524)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b2d4c14e-18f7-4c2e-b148-8e4cd2fec3ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "after training, the three embeddings are still one shared array"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6fdab1c1-d5b8-45da-a266-d490d2b4472d"],

Cell["4. Decoding and checking", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"81796c4a-1050-4a3e-b806-efce3cf4cf6c"],

Cell["\<\
Each test source is decoded three ways: greedy (a beam of width 1) with no \
constraint; a beam of width 4 with the length penalty \[Alpha] = 0.6 and no \
constraint; and the same beam constrained by the prefix grammar, which allows \
</s> only when the tree is complete and nothing else then. Every answer is \
checked by the oracle. As in Lample and Charton, 'any in beam' counts a \
source as solved if any hypothesis in the beam passes the check.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d71fdb5-54c9-4303-a30a-309c56fbf68d"],

